{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina","id":811316,"title":"Estimating Stamina","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-18T14:18:12-08:00","id":811316,"title":"Estimating Stamina","content":"So! I kind of glossed over this at first, but feeding more than two points of Vitae on average is going to really mess people up.<br /> <br /> Effectively: Taking more Vitae than someone's Stamina gives them Drained. If one assumes an average of 2, that means 2 safe Vitae per vessel.<br /> <br /> Drained is brutal. -2 to all physical actions as well as rolls to stabilize and survive injury. Physical effort requires a Stamina roll or you pass out for an hour or more. They count being fed from (!), taking damage, or spending Willpower on a physical roll here. This means that your prey may well pass out once you take a point of Vitae beyond their stamina.<br /> <br /> It lasts until all Lethal damage is healed through normal means. This means you may very well leave your vessel unable to do their job (depending on how physical it is) or defend themselves for a week (three lethal/six days) if they pass out at the earliest time for the average individual. Easily longer if you feed more.<br /> <br /> In short, while it may not be everyone's interpretation, I'd qualify feeding this much as a Breaking Point for &quot;Causing Harm for Blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which leads to the question: Can Vampires tell when they are about to take too much blood? Is there a roll to estimate a target's Stamina so you know which are more likely to handle feeding better (and thus provide more safe Vitae)? Am I the only person who puts this much thought into it, or have other people put thought into handling this? Or do you just let people feed blind and make them roll if they take too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T15:02:08-08:00","id":811343,"title":"","content":"They ain't mortals anymore so they'll have to gather some Intel on the issue. I did my homework and I came up with this.<br /> <br /> Hemorrhaging is broken down into four classes by the American College of Surgeons' advanced trauma life support (ATLS).<br /> <br /> Class I Hemorrhage involves up to 15% of blood volume. There is typically no change in vital signs and fluid resuscitation is not usually necessary.<br /> <br /> Class II Hemorrhage involves 15-30% of total blood volume. A patient is often tachycardic (rapid heart beat) with a narrowing of the difference between the systolic and diastolic blood pressures. The body attempts to compensate with peripheral vasoconstriction. Skin may start to look pale and be cool to the touch. The patient may exhibit slight changes in behavior. Volume resuscitation with crystalloids (Saline solution or Lactated Ringer's solution) is all that is typically required. Blood transfusion is not typically required.<br /> <br /> Class III Hemorrhage involves loss of 30-40% of circulating blood volume. The patient's blood pressure drops, the heart rate increases, peripheral hypoperfusion (shock), such as capillary refill worsens, and the mental status worsens. Fluid resuscitation with crystalloid and blood transfusion are usually necessary.<br /> <br /> Class IV Hemorrhage involves loss of &gt;40% of circulating blood volume. The limit of the body's compensation is reached and aggressive resuscitation is required to prevent death.<br /> This system is basically the same as used in the staging of hypovolemic shock.<br /> <br /> Individuals in excellent physical and cardiovascular shape may have more effective compensatory mechanisms before experiencing cardiovascular collapse. These patients may look deceptively stable, with minimal derangements in vital signs, while having poor peripheral perfusion. Elderly patients or those with chronic medical conditions may have less tolerance to blood loss, less ability to compensate, and may take medications such as betablockers that can potentially blunt the cardiovascular response. Care must be taken in the assessment of these patients.<br /> <br /> For Vampire:<br /> <br /> Class 1: one BP, 2 if the victim is very healthy (4+ Stamina rating or a special merit)<br /> Class 2: two BPs, three is the victim is very healthy <br /> Class 3: three BPs, four is the victim is very healthy: if left unattended, roll a chance die; on a one victim dies <br /> Class 4: four BPs or five if the victim is very healthy: left unattended victim dies, if taken care of by an ER team, roll stamina, failure meaning death<br /> Class 5: five BPs or 6 if the victim is very healthy: victim dies<br /> <br /> Children, elderly people or adults with 1 stamina are more exposed: worsen their condition by one threshold (taking one BP from a kid would generate a class two situation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T16:57:51-08:00","id":811384,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I roll randomly per victim unless it's someone specific.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">1 = One Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2-4 = Two Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3-7 Three Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">8-9 = Four Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">10 = Five Stamina</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Simple Medicine, Survival or Brawl check lets them learn their Stamina. Player chooses how many points to take, consequences ensue. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T17:01:32-08:00","id":811388,"title":"","content":"I'd say a vampire with a little experience is capable of estimating how much blood they can take. It's probably going to be based less on how much they themselves gulp down as paying attention to how the person they're feeding on is responding. Pulse rate, general level of awakeness, that kind of thing. As a Storyteller, I have no problem with a player saying &quot;I take as many points as I can without endangering them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T17:16:32-08:00","id":811399,"title":"","content":"All very useful information. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T20:29:30-08:00","id":811508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=811388#post811388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say a vampire with a little experience is capable of estimating how much blood they can take. It's probably going to be based less on how much they themselves gulp down as paying attention to how the person they're feeding on is responding. Pulse rate, general level of awakeness, that kind of thing. As a Storyteller, I have no problem with a player saying &quot;I take as many points as I can without endangering them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I also consider that a vampire feeding from humans don't really take a substantial volume of the victim's blood (barring gruesome feeding habits such as Coils or Cru\u00e1c), but actually their life-force with it. It's why it's called Vitae in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T21:07:54-08:00","id":811526,"title":"","content":"If you really want to roll for it, something like a reflexive Wits + Medicine roll seems like a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T21:49:51-08:00","id":811544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=811508#post811508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. I also consider that a vampire feeding from humans don't really take a substantial volume of the victim's blood (barring gruesome feeding habits such as Coils or Cru\u00e1c), but actually their life-force with it. It's why it's called Vitae in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was speaking specifically to the Drained condition rather than actual volume of blood loss. I actually agree with you here. I'm of the opinion that a vampire can drain a person of Vitae and kill them and still leave plenty of blood in their system. Draining people dry makes no sense. All that blood has to go somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T07:46:05-08:00","id":812597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=811544#post811544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I was speaking specifically to the Drained condition rather than actual volume of blood loss. I actually agree with you here. I'm of the opinion that a vampire can drain a person of Vitae and kill them and still leave plenty of blood in their system. Draining people dry makes no sense. All that blood has to go somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This confuses me a little here. Blood -becomes- vitae once it is inside a vampire. Humans dont contain vitae. Blood is not vitae this is true, but a vampire drinks blood and turns it into vitae. drinking a human's blood causes 1L per vitae you want.. I would say that if you fill the human's boxes with Lethal damage they will likely die from the blood loss unless you get them to the hospital, but wouldnt necessarily be &quot;dry&quot; unless you full aggravated them.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would think a vampire who feeds off a mortal enough knows their limit and can safely not give them the drained condition. Also I think any vampire paying attention to heart rate and makes an effort to not take too much can leave their victims not drained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 01-20-2016, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T07:57:55-08:00","id":812608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=811544#post811544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I was speaking specifically to the Drained condition rather than actual volume of blood loss. I actually agree with you here. I'm of the opinion that a vampire can drain a person of Vitae and kill them and still leave plenty of blood in their system. Draining people dry makes no sense. All that blood has to go somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But does it? Vampire don't work like physical creatures, their fangs hurts a lot not because they're big and sharp but because they are mysticaly symbolic of danger. Vampire blood is denser and syrupy when vitae is present in their system. fact is they do drink blood and enough of it to cause serious blood loss. But why should that blood have to go anywhere? It's consumed, mysticly distilled into vitae inside the vampire body. Kindred laugh at physical laws of conservation of mass and thermodynamic. Why is it conceptualy easier to think, against provided rules, that vampire drain something from the body but not really that much blood, rather than think that yes, they do drain that much blood but it doesn't have to go anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T08:29:06-08:00","id":812627,"title":"","content":"By RAW, a human can lose 6 points of lethal to feeding and not die. Therefore, 6 pointsworth of blood is approximately what a human can lose and not die. Which means it can't be more than 40%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:22:58-08:00","id":812668,"title":"","content":"What page number is that on? Because I am thinking the guy with 5 stamina could give 10 vitae before he dies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:29:47-08:00","id":812675,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I meant to say an <i>average</i> human. At 7 health 6 lethal is not going to kill you by itself. Therefore it must logically be equivalent to a volume of blood that losing won't kill you by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:39:00-08:00","id":812680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=812675#post812675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I meant to say an <i>average</i> human. At 7 health 6 lethal is not going to kill you by itself. Therefore it must logically be equivalent to a volume of blood that losing won't kill you by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't entirely follow. Equating blood volume with leath damage taken is more than problematic given that a 5'2, hundred pounds soaking wet person can have stamina 5 and therefore ccould lose more blood than a 7 foot 300 punds giant with low stamina. Despite the smaller person having less blood than the bigger one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:41:01-08:00","id":812682,"title":"","content":"I cheat and just have a general rule of thumb that I pass around as an open secret among the Kindred in my city. &quot;Count to five, then let go.&quot; That's two turns of general sucking, roughly 2 BP. Its something I imagine that would become kind of a way of understanding how much is generally safe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:43:09-08:00","id":812684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=812668#post812668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What page number is that on? Because I am thinking the guy with 5 stamina could give 10 vitae before he dies...</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, he could give 15. When you're full lethal, you're not dead. Dying, but not dead. You can keep on sucking blood, and get more vitae. After 10 lethal, he upgrades a point of lethal every round, plus the continual sucking keeps going at once a round. Meaning it will take 5 rounds of sucking before completely dead. With magic involved to stabilize, that'd be a total of 20 vitae in someone with Stamina 5 and no Giant merit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:48:45-08:00","id":812689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=811384#post811384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I roll randomly per victim unless it's someone specific.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">1 = One Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2-4 = Two Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3-7 Three Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">8-9 = Four Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">10 = Five Stamina</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Simple Medicine, Survival or Brawl check lets them learn their Stamina. Player chooses how many points to take, consequences ensue. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Random roll like this ^ to give the NPC stamina is perfect.<br /> <br /> I also like to go by the feeding successes too. If you got 3 successes.. you can safely take 3.<br /> There are many ways to go about this.<br /> <br /> To try and figure out actual quantities of blood taken, I feel, totally takes away from the game at hand. either have the ST roll.. or roll for your feed. Choose to give your victim the drained condition or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  Original statement proved true 01-21-2016, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:47:02-08:00","id":812970,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not really relevant, but I've always interpreted Vitae as Life energy. It seems a given since that's what the word means. Plus the fact that animals with more blood than humans can give less Vitae, and blood from Corpses gives none at all unless extremely fresh. Plus, given people with higher Stamina can provide more Vitae before they die, but humans all have roughly the same amount of Blood, makes me really think that the blood is just where Vampires can sift it from, and healthier people have more of it in the same amount of blood. Similarly, older vampires don't store physically more Vitae. Elders are just able to concentrate it down. Kind of like those kool-aid packets. A Neonate is filling a pitcher and following the directions. Ancillae might be using half as much water to fill the pitcher. An Elder at 10 BP is just filling the pitcher with koolaid powder.<br /> <br /> So given that fact, assuming that all vitae = all blood (rather than just the point where they have no life (vitae) left and are therefore dead and useless for feeding) seems a little silly and makes it a lot harder to maintain Masquerade.<br /> <br /> In short, Vampires are drinking life force through the medium of blood. The blood is just secondary. The Drained condition, the Lethal damage, all of that represent loss of life force more accurately than loss of blood. That's my interpretation. Nobody else has to follow it, it just makes most sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:57:18-08:00","id":812974,"title":"","content":"The number of vitae you can pull form someone with 10 health is 10. You can't keep draining them any further to do aggravate, because there's nothing left to drain, mojo-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:36:35-08:00","id":813040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=812974#post812974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The number of vitae you can pull form someone with 10 health is 10. You can't keep draining them any further to do aggravate, because there's nothing left to drain, mojo-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. There's no rule stating how much Vitae a human has, only that every point of Vitae taken causes one point of lethal damage to a human vessel. A person full on lethal can continue taking lethal damage, so I don't see any reason they couldn't also keep providing Vitae. If you define Vitae as life force, well they're still alive right up until they're full on aggravated damage, so why wouldn't there be any mojo left?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:30:00-08:00","id":813138,"title":"","content":"The idea of them draining more &quot;energy&quot; than blood makes sense to me. It helps maintain the Masquerade, especially since you won't strictly be finding bloodless corpses all the time, and it does so in such a way that makes the Masquerade a bit more plausible. It also means that the recently previewed Psychic Vampires are closer to proper Kindred than I previously assumed and that's awesome.<br /> <br /> I imagine that actually draining blood is an indulgent or luxurious feeding style for Kindred. Actually exsanguinating a human means that either you aren't possessed of the restraint and composure to uphold the Masquerade or that you're such a distinguished member of the Danse Macabre that you can afford to dispose of the bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:35:52-08:00","id":813143,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the whole &quot;Vitae is life energy, blood is the agent that bears it&quot; thing is cannon. That's also how Strix are able to gain Vitae through breath - same fuel, different medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T01:38:40-08:00","id":813242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kindred can pull a number of Vitae from a mortal equal to the mortal\u2019s unmodified Health dots. </div> </div> </div>That was not an interpretation. That was literally what the book says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T05:05:52-08:00","id":813292,"title":"","content":"Absolutely its true. The thing about the CofD that I really like is that almost everything is a kind of metaphor. So, yes, blood is a symbol for life energy. You're sucking out their life energy with the blood. <br /> <br /> Of course, it being a metaphor, you're draining someone of life energy at the same time you're draining someone of blood. The two are instrictly linked. So, when we talk about draining someone of life energy, its a matter of course that they're going to be drained of physical blood as well. That's kind of how metaphors work. <br /> <br /> Yes, leaving around corpses half drained of blood is a threat to the Masquerade since its a sign of sloppy vampire feeding. And that's a good thing from a story perspective - you want more of that risk of creating hunters, you want that drama in the game.<br /> <br /> All this is my opinion, anyways. YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:05:15-08:00","id":813314,"title":"","content":"Leaving around corpses half drained of blood is also a threat to the masquerade because they have a bad habit of getting up and eating people by themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T10:16:38-08:00","id":813463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=813242#post813242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was not an interpretation. That was literally what the book says.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I missed that. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T10:51:17-08:00","id":813484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=813138#post813138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine that actually draining blood is an indulgent or luxurious feeding style for Kindred. Actually exsanguinating a human means that either you aren't possessed of the restraint and composure to uphold the Masquerade or that you're such a distinguished member of the Danse Macabre that you can afford to dispose of the bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cannon: Page 98 <br /> &quot; <i>Vitae is not blood; at least, not directly. Kindred create Vitae<br /> as a byproduct of processing the blood they absorb. There\u2019s no<br /> digestion; the blood seeps through the gullet and washes through<br /> decaying tissues.</i> &quot;<br /> <br /> You actually drain blood. It's not metaphoric. It's literal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:18:41-07:00","id":864522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=812680#post812680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't entirely follow. Equating blood volume with lethal damage taken is more than problematic given that a 5'2, hundred pounds soaking wet person can have stamina 5 and therefore could lose more blood than a 7 foot 300 punds giant with low stamina. Despite the smaller person having less blood than the bigger one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolute volume of blood sure, but wasn't the person you quoted (Elfies) speaking in percentages, and it stand to reason the larger you are the more absolute volume of blood you'd need to survive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfies</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By RAW, a human can lose 6 points of lethal to feeding and not die. Therefore, 6 points-worth of blood is approximately what a human can lose and not die. Which means it can't be more than 40%.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18332802\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18332802</a><br /> <br /> And the percentages seem to check out, though ability to resist going into shock also seems to be a factor.<br /> <br /> I would also point out at 7 health levels for an average human they begin to &quot;bleed out&quot; which could be interpreted as going into shock or internal hemorrhaging but clearly isn't a complete lack of blood (because they can be stabilized, and people completely lacking blood can't be stabilized without a transfusion). I would agree that drinking a human down all the way to the last Aggravated Damage would be draining them dry.<br /> <br /> This makes a normal human a 14 Vitae meal, potentially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 04-12-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:41:35-07:00","id":864584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina?p=864522#post864522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would also point out at 7 health levels for an average human they begin to &quot;bleed out&quot; which could be interpreted as going into shock or internal hemorrhaging but clearly isn't a complete lack of blood (because they can be stabilized, and people completely lacking blood can't be stabilized without a transfusion). I would agree that drinking a human down all the way to the last Aggravated Damage would be draining them dry.<br /> <br /> This makes a normal human a 14 Vitae meal, potentially.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> RAW:<br /> &quot; Human blood is best warm, from the living. <b>Kindred can<br /> pull a number of Vitae from a mortal equal to the mortal\u2019s<br /> unmodified Health dots. </b>Every point of Vitae she takes causes<br /> one point of lethal damage. If she takes more Vitae than the<br /> human has dots of Stamina, he suffers the Drained Condition<br /> (see p. 303). Once a vampire attains her sixth dot of Blood<br /> Potency, she no longer finds human blood nourishing. &quot;<br /> <br /> As Elfive already pointed out.<br /> <br /> The average human is at 7 .. you can get 7.<br /> <br /> The max for a human is 10 ( baring some merits or whatevers added) You can get 10 .<br /> <br /> If you want more than that. you need producer merit. which is 2V for 1L","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-12-2016, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}